1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,545
This is GTM Handoff Reliability Desk, an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

2
00:00:05,595 --> 00:00:07,700
It is not affiliated with Dust.

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:13,610
Every record is synthetic, and every CRM write and read is simulated in this browser.

4
00:00:14,501 --> 00:00:16,943
First, a file with the wrong header.

5
00:00:16,993 --> 00:00:20,611
The import is refused, and nothing reaches the queue.

6
00:00:21,471 --> 00:00:23,171
Now the synthetic export.

7
00:00:23,221 --> 00:00:23,731
19 rows.

8
00:00:23,781 --> 00:00:30,171
One row has a bad email and a timestamp with no offset, so it is rejected by row and column.

9
00:00:30,221 --> 00:00:35,071
Deduplicating by stable ID leaves 15 records, and 7 packets are ready.

10
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:38,249
The queue shows why each record stopped.

11
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:41,742
Rows 3 and 17 share a record ID, so they merge.

12
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:46,276
Two leads with the same name but different IDs stay separate.

13
00:00:46,532 --> 00:00:50,897
A lead from Brazil has no territory rule, so it is refused, not guessed.

14
00:00:50,947 --> 00:00:54,882
Conflicting owners go to a person, and the current owner is kept.

15
00:00:55,137 --> 00:00:58,582
This handoff has no confirmed budget and no champion.

16
00:00:58,632 --> 00:01:03,527
It cannot advance, the missing fields are listed, and approval is disabled.

17
00:01:03,972 --> 00:01:10,054
A clean UK handoff exports a source-backed packet for the native Dust agent, GTMHandoffBrief.

18
00:01:10,104 --> 00:01:12,362
The email is reduced to its domain.

19
00:01:12,612 --> 00:01:17,192
Next, the real native agent, GTMHandoffBrief, in Ayo's Dust workspace.

20
00:01:17,242 --> 00:01:21,028
These are actual native preview captures, shown as stills.

21
00:01:21,078 --> 00:01:25,412
For the clean packet, it drafts a brief for the routed owner.

22
00:01:25,462 --> 00:01:28,742
Every context line cites a source from the packet.

23
00:01:28,792 --> 00:01:35,342
For the missing evidence packet, it refuses, and lists both missing fields: budget confirmed and champion.

24
00:01:35,392 --> 00:01:39,842
For the ownership conflict, it refuses too, and drafts nothing.

25
00:01:40,235 --> 00:01:43,075
Back in the desk, the real reply is pasted in.

26
00:01:43,125 --> 00:01:48,100
It is labelled pasted, provenance not verified, because no adapter is connected.

27
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:52,812
The desk checks it against the same packet, and it passes with zero errors.

28
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:59,345
As a negative control, a labelled fixture with an invented source is rejected, naming the rule it broke.

29
00:02:00,219 --> 00:02:03,538
A person approves, and their name and time are recorded.

30
00:02:03,588 --> 00:02:09,194
The simulated HubSpot write then sets the owner and creates one task under an idempotency key.

31
00:02:09,244 --> 00:02:14,369
Replaying the approval and the write changes nothing: the log shows two no-op replays.

32
00:02:15,997 --> 00:02:19,987
A simulated fresh read confirms the owner, and exactly one task.

33
00:02:20,842 --> 00:02:22,396
Finally, reporting.

34
00:02:22,446 --> 00:02:28,222
Overall conversion rises from 17.5% to 30.75%, yet every source fell.

35
00:02:28,272 --> 00:02:31,852
It is a mix shift, so no impact is claimed.

36
00:02:32,716 --> 00:02:38,307
Every decision exports as a spec and a regression case that replays exactly.

37
00:02:38,357 --> 00:02:39,866
Concept by Ayo Ahmed.

